{"name":"Beacon Yellow","hex":"#f2c98a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beacon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A signal fire to notify of the approach of an enemy, or to give any notice, commonly of warning.","A signal, buoy, post, or other conspicuous mark erected on an eminence near the shore, or moored in shoal water, as a guide to mariners, particularly to warn vessels of danger."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act as a beacon.","To give light to, as a beacon; to light up; to illumine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beacon"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beacon","blocks":[{"text":"A beacon is an intentionally conspicuous device designed to attract attention to a specific location. A common example is the lighthouse, which draws attention to a fixed point that can be used to navigate around obstacles or into port. More modern examples include a variety of radio beacons that can be read on radio direction finders in all weather, and radar transponders that appear on radar displays."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beacon","wikidata":"Q7321258"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Beacon_at_Orontes_Bank.jpg/500px-Beacon_at_Orontes_Bank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Beacon_at_Orontes_Bank.jpg/1280px-Beacon_at_Orontes_Bank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Beacon_at_Orontes_Bank.jpg/500px-Beacon_at_Orontes_Bank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A navigational beacon denoting the presence of Orontes Bank off Port Vincent, South Australia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeacon_at_Orontes_Bank.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Culmstock%2C_Culmstock_Beacon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_213525.jpg/500px-Culmstock%2C_Culmstock_Beacon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_213525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Culmstock%2C_Culmstock_Beacon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_213525.jpg/500px-Culmstock%2C_Culmstock_Beacon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_